            <ArticleTitle>Pattern of Sexually Transmitted Diseases in and Around Udaipur.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>90-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The patients who attended the STD clinic of our hospital during the last 10 years were studied retrospectively to work out the pattern of major sexually transmitted diseases viz. -syphilis, ionorrhoea, chancroid, lymphogranuloma vencreum and donovinosis. The total number of patients was 1093, The relative incidence of chancroid was found. higher (37.78%) than syphilis (32.47%), gonorrhoea (24 79%) mixed infections (3.38%), donovanosis (1.18%) and lymphogranuloma venereum (0.36%).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
